<title>NORWAY: Saga Petroleum 8-month pre-tax rises.</title>
<headline>Saga Petroleum 8-month pre-tax rises.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Eight months to August 31.</p>
<p>				  (millions of crowns unless stated)</p>
<p>Operating result	     1,968     vs	  1,295</p>
<p>Pre-tax result		 2,121     vs	  1,195</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of Norway's largest private oil company is Saga Petroleum ASA. A Reuter poll of eight analysts forecast an operating profit of 1.90 billion crowns and a result before tax of 2.08 billion crowns. Three of the analysts recommended a buy on the share, three said hold, one said sell and one declined to provide a recommendation.  </p>
<p>Operating income	     4,666     vs	  3,697</p>
<p>Operating costs		2,698     vs	  2,402</p>
<p>After-tax result		 792     vs	    352</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
